  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "President Prabowo Subianto has officially indicated that he is beginning the search for a new vice president to replace Gibran. This development follows recent public remarks where the president noted the urgency of the situation, stating he has no time for rest as he attends to this leadership vacancy. Political parties across the spectrum have begun responding to the announcement. Some, such as the National Mandate Party (PAN) and the Prosperous Justice Party (PKS), have stated they will not be putting forward internal candidates to fill the position, citing respect for the president’s decision-making process. Other organizations, including the National Awakening Party (PKB), have suggested that the ideal successor should possess a strong history of collaboration with the president. The administration is expected to focus on the selection process following the president's travel schedule, which includes visits to Manila and Shenzhen.",
